cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this pipeline, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Structure-Based Virtual Screening Pipeline"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-14"
authors:
  - family-names: Ali
    given-names: Shahid
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4724-5086"
    affiliation: "School of Biology, Hunan University, Changsha, China"
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ali-jarvis/vs-pipeline"
url: "https://github.com/Ali-jarvis/vs-pipeline"
abstract: >
  A reproducible, scheduler-free pipeline for structure-based virtual screening
  of large small-molecule libraries against a protein target. Uses RDKit and
  Meeko for ligand preparation, AutoDock Vina for parallel docking on a single
  server, custom parsers for ranked CSV output and top-hit extraction, and a
  PyMOL script for publication-quality 3D interaction figures.
keywords:
  - virtual screening
  - AutoDock Vina
  - structure-based drug discovery
  - cheminformatics
  - RDKit
  - Meeko
  - PyMOL
